1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,002
MarketNavi comes with a library of Groups and Sets,

2
00:00:03,022 --> 00:00:05,633
built around common trading situations.

3
00:00:05,683 --> 00:00:08,671
In Prism, open Provided by MarketNavi.

4
00:00:50,547 --> 00:00:53,450
Each one shows small icons for what it looks at.

5
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:57,277
Here: volume, and structure, the support and resistance levels.

6
00:00:57,714 --> 00:01:01,321
Underneath, one line says what it describes, in plain words.

7
00:01:01,762 --> 00:01:03,641
Tap more for three parts:

8
00:01:03,691 --> 00:01:05,143
what it measures,

9
00:01:05,193 --> 00:01:06,986
why traders watch it,

10
00:01:07,036 --> 00:01:08,808
and what it doesn't prove.

11
00:01:09,244 --> 00:01:11,827
The last icon is the evidence mark.

12
00:01:11,877 --> 00:01:14,310
A microscope means not yet studied.

13
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:17,945
A balance means it was studied, and showed no clear difference.

14
00:01:17,995 --> 00:01:20,343
The next two videos explain both.

15
00:01:20,775 --> 00:01:24,083
To find one quickly, tap an icon in the filter row.

16
00:01:24,133 --> 00:01:26,886
Here, only the Sets that look at volatility.

17
00:01:27,331 --> 00:01:32,004
Tap plus, and a provided Set becomes one of your Prism scans, ready to run.

18
00:01:32,449 --> 00:01:35,864
Every provided Set is built from the same blocks you use.

19
00:01:35,914 --> 00:01:38,582
Look inside shows them, in plain words.

20
00:01:38,632 --> 00:01:41,189
Make my own copy opens it in Signal Sets,

21
00:01:41,209 --> 00:01:44,841
to change and save as yours; its study comes with it.

22
00:02:03,097 --> 00:02:06,832
Signal Groups and Signal Sets have the same library at the top.

23
00:02:06,882 --> 00:02:11,000
And the Start from list offers them too, after New, and before your own.

24
00:02:11,894 --> 00:02:15,373
Once you know them, one setting hides everything provided.

25
00:02:15,423 --> 00:02:17,792
Descriptive readings, not advice.
